# New files are ignored by default, so nothing gets committed by accident:
# an app folder moved into a package can carry tokens, history or account
# details. Files git already tracks aren't affected. Add a new one on
# purpose, one file at a time (-f skips these rules, so never use it on a
# folder):
#
#   dots add -f common/.config/foo/foo.conf

# Ignore every file...
*

# ...but not folders: git refuses even `git add` on a tracked file inside an
# ignored folder
!*/
